/*
 * Declares the CompoundType class.
 *
 * A CompoundType represents any native type composed of multiple inner types.
 * Examples include arrays, maps, slices, tuples, ranges, futures, and other
 * built-in aggregate types. Each compound type stores its constituent types
 * in the `inners` list, and derives its semantic behavior from them.
 *
 * Compound types are defined by the language itself and form part of the
 * native type hierarchy. They are not user-defined aggregates(such as classes
 * or records), but built-in structural types with fixed semantics.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::type::native::compound
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/type/native/compound.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-12-06
